Subject: libipa, sensor: Add IMX320 and IMX345

The Snapdragon Galaxy S9 uses a Sony IMX320 front and IMX345 rear sensor.
Without a helper the SoftISP cannot convert between gain code and gain, so
its AGC never raises the analogue gain and every frame comes out black.

Both use the usual Sony gain = 1024 / (1024 - code) model, the same as the
IMX477 and IMX708, and their black level was measured at 64 in 10 bits.

Neither sensor is in the properties database, so libcamera warns that it is
"assuming unverified defaults" and uses a gain delay of one frame. Every
other Sony sensor in the database except the imx219 and imx283 applies gain
two frames later, and assuming one frame makes the AGC correct against a
frame that has not taken the previous correction yet -- the loop then
overshoots on a scene change and clips.

Pixel pitches are from the Galaxy S9, which pairs a 1.4um rear IMX345 with a
1.22um front IMX320. The delays follow the Sony family convention rather than
individual measurement.
---
 src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp       | 24 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../sensor/camera_sensor_properties.cpp       | 20 ++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 44 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp b/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp
index 359040ec7..4c2c5d0be 100644
--- a/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp
+++ b/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp
@@ -599,6 +599,18 @@ public:
 };
 REGISTER_CAMERA_SENSOR_HELPER("imx296", CameraSensorHelperImx296)
 
+class CameraSensorHelperImx320 : public CameraSensorHelper
+{
+public:
+	CameraSensorHelperImx320()
+	{
+		/* Measured on hardware: 64 at 10 bits. */
+		blackLevel_ = 4096;
+		gain_ = AnalogueGainLinear{ 0, 1024, -1, 1024 };
+	}
+};
+REGISTER_CAMERA_SENSOR_HELPER("imx320", CameraSensorHelperImx320)
+
